@node Abbreviation learning
@section Abbreviation learning

When you correct a misspelled word through Jinx's correction
interface@comma{} @samp{jinx-extras.el} automatically defines an abbreviation in
@code{text-mode-abbrev-table} mapping the misspelled word to its
correction.  From that point on@comma{} typing the same misspelling in any
@code{text-mode}-derived buffer triggers automatic expansion to the correct
word (provided @code{abbrev-mode} is active).

This is implemented via @samp{:before} advice on the internal Jinx
function @code{jinx--correct-replace}.  The advice extracts the original
misspelled text from the Jinx overlay@comma{} pairs it with the selected
correction@comma{} and calls @code{define-abbrev}.  A confirmation message is
displayed in the echo area for each new abbreviation.

Over time this builds a personalized typo-correction dictionary that
speeds up writing without any manual configuration.

@node One GLib in Emacsapp
@section One GLib in Emacs.app

@vindex jinx-extras-relink-program
Jinx's module links Homebrew's enchant@comma{} which links Homebrew's GLib.
The @samp{emacs-plus-app} build of Emacs bundles its own GLib in
@samp{Emacs.app/Contents/Frameworks}@comma{} so loading the module puts a second
GLib into Emacs@comma{} and Emacs prints at every start: ``Class
GNotificationCenterDelegate is implemented in both @dots{} This may cause
spurious casting failures and mysterious crashes.''

Before Jinx loads its module@comma{} @samp{jinx-extras.el} checks with @samp{otool}
whether the module links Homebrew's enchant.  If it does@comma{} it runs
@code{jinx-extras-relink-program} (@samp{bin/jinx-enchant-relink} in the
dotfiles)@comma{} which copies enchant and its provider plugins to
@samp{~/.local/lib/jinx-enchant/}@comma{} points their GLib references at the
copies Emacs.app already has loaded@comma{} and relinks the module to that
copy.  When Jinx has just compiled a new module@comma{} the relink runs right
after loading it@comma{} so the fix takes effect at the next start.  Set the
option to nil to turn this off.

Run the program by hand after @samp{brew upgrade enchant} or an
@samp{emacs-plus-app} update@comma{} since an existing relinked module does not
trigger it again.

